{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443318-how-would-you-get-a-v5-player-into-v20","id":1443318,"title":"How Would You Get A V5 player into V20?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-04-09T18:53:46-07:00","id":1443318,"title":"How Would You Get A V5 player into V20?","content":"I\u2019ve only played Vampire 5th edition. However, I was thinking of getting into 20th Anniversary, but I am very intimidated by the massive chunk in mechanics. Is there any real reason to try out 20th when we have 5th edition? I know there are many people who hate 5th edition. However, I do not know why personally. Is there something 20th edition does better?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-09T18:57:14-07:00","id":1443320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443318-how-would-you-get-a-v5-player-into-v20#post1443318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019ve only played Vampire 5th edition. However, I was thinking of getting into 20th Anniversary, but I am very intimidated by the massive chunk in mechanics. Is there any real reason to try out 20th when we have 5th edition? I know there are many people who hate 5th edition. However, I do not know why personally. Is there something 20th edition does better?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's primarily lore changes that irritate people.<br /> <br /> V20 does have better blood mechanics for management wise as a general rule. Hunger Frenzies and feeding is much easier as even Elders can usually feed on Animal Blood.<br /> <br /> Blood points are also less likely to backfire than Rouse checks.<br /> <br /> Thin Bloods are also more powerful.<br /> <br /> Humanity is much-much easier to lose but Paths exist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-10-2021, 11:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-09T20:06:37-07:00","id":1443330,"title":"","content":"I personally prefer v5 but i would switch to v20 to play an elder game. V20 has great options if you also want to have everything at your fingertips for character creation options. Every bloodline discipline? All there with easy access<br /> No need to house rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3901-radiofreedeath","name":"RadioFreeDeath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-09T23:55:42-07:00","id":1443340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443318-how-would-you-get-a-v5-player-into-v20#post1443318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019ve only played Vampire 5th edition. However, I was thinking of getting into 20th Anniversary, but I am very intimidated by the massive chunk in mechanics. Is there any real reason to try out 20th when we have 5th edition? I know there are many people who hate 5th edition. However, I do not know why personally. Is there something 20th edition does better?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> V20 (and previous editions, with which it is broadly compatible) lack the Hunger mechanics which play such a large role in V5. Blood Pool is somewhat more straightforward, but makes the Feeding process more anodyne. If you find Hunger gets annoying, V20 will be far more liberating (some complain that it leads to &quot;superheroes with fangs&quot; style play as using Disciplines/boosting Attributes is much less risky). On the other hand, Humanity in V20 is more rigid---certain actions always carry the risk of Degeneration, whereas in V5 you're more free to set Tenets according to the thematic needs of your Chronicle and your vision for your character. I'm not going to call one &quot;better&quot; than the other but, cards on the table, I prefer V20's approach and find V5's Hunger to be frustratingly limiting. In some ways V5 characters are more flexible out the gate as it's easier to create characters with Out-of-Clan Disciplines, but the required Drawbacks/Flaws and the requirement to choose a Feeding Preference force you into a stereotype which V20 doesn't. Characters in V20 (it seems to me) are much more striated than in V5. An 8th Generation Vampire can WRECK high-generation enemies, whereas Blood Potency has a more shallow power curve. Merits and Flaws are totally optional in V20 and can be ignored altogether if you don't want to fuss with them. Creating and managing Ghouls and other minions is also much less of a headache. Again, I won't try to persuade you one approach is better than the other--overall, V5 mechanically reinforces the difficulties of being a vampire much more strongly while V20 gives you more freedom and higher plateaus to reach but can be overwhelming with its sheer number of options (unless your ST imposes some limitations, as I always do).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26710,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26710-ventrue-busboy","user":"Ventrue Busboy","date":". 04-10-2021, 03:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26710-ventrue-busboy","name":"Ventrue Busboy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26710_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-10T00:51:45-07:00","id":1443344,"title":"","content":"V20 has simpler disciplines, simpler factions, simpler character creation, simpler humanity, simpler backgrounds, a more honest assessment of easier-to-use skills, but more complicated combat (House rules: Ignore initiative phase, and take half for damage/soak do a lot to cut down on combat, which is largely intuitive but very slow) I'd argue that the disciplines and factions are better written too, and though I acknowledge that's a subjective thing, it'd be a hill I'd die on. <br /> <br /> The only problem I'd say is that V20 presents all all the major clans and their disciplines as equal, when they're not. Without looking bloodline section of the book, you're shown 13 clans and all their disciplines, A new Camarilla player should only really look at 7 clans and the common disciplines (That they use if you want to be cut things down further) Protean and perhaps thaumaturgy. Looking at the Tzmisce is no good if you're wanting to play a cam game for the first time. Don't be fooled; the game might have a lot more disciplines than v5, but they're streamlined and so much easier to work with than the convoluted discipline system V5 has. <br /> <br /> The only thing V5 improves on is... uh... Disciplines are more balanced in comparison to eachother. One thing to consider is that V5 is very much a game that tries to liberate you; big overpowering organizations are weakened, there's lots of room to advance; anarchs are just as good, if not better than the cam; you can play a Tremere without having a giant fucking pyramid behind you. It certainly doesn't always work, since you had much more freedom with morality in prior editions, you weren't bound by touchstones, and you didn't have to worry nearly as much about discipline builds in prior editions, but the general gist is to make V5 politically 'Easy'. V1,2,3 and 20, however, give you the Jyhad; Push, push, struggle: You will always have elders trying to keep you down and when you're older you'll have plucky neonates trying to eat you to get up. The Camarilla is a hegemony and you'll only join the anarchs if you can't cut it. You're under pressure, and it's good. <br /> Also there's the Sabbat who're just super interesting. <br /> <br /> You might actually want to have a look at the first edition of vampire. It's not so big and intimidating as V20, but is fully compatible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-10T03:49:15-07:00","id":1443352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443318-how-would-you-get-a-v5-player-into-v20#post1443318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019ve only played Vampire 5th edition. However, I was thinking of getting into 20th Anniversary, but I am very intimidated by the massive chunk in mechanics. Is there any real reason to try out 20th when we have 5th edition? I know there are many people who hate 5th edition. However, I do not know why personally. Is there something 20th edition does better?</div> </div> </div> </div>Everything? In my experience at least. To be fair I've played VtM 1/2/Rev/20th for almost 30 years and V5 for only 6 months but the only sort of game where I'd use V5 over the others would be a one shot shovelhead game where the PCs were newly mass embraced with no idea how to handle their new existence. The Hunger system would work well to represent the lack of control and random outbursts that newborns can experience but it doesn't model more experienced vampires well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-10T06:47:33-07:00","id":1443363,"title":"","content":"I would say the biggest selling point of V20 is that it's far more flexible than V5. V5 is designed with a much tighter range of what play should look like (even with the book trying to toss out a lot of options). V20 can handle a much wider range of both playstyles and subject matter. <br /> <br /> V20's mechanics are dated, and there's certainly some bloat to it (remembering that V20 was first planned as a one-off omnibus edition not a major revision), but they're a more solid foundation. The big divide here is basically V20's more utilitarian approach where things basically work as intended but can feel a bit heavy, vs. V5's attempts to be more evocative (which people have very strong subjective responses to) at the cost of some really glaring iffy results once you run into them.<br /> <br /> Lore-wise, if you don't have a big connection to the deep lore of VtM, it's not that big of a deal. Again, I think V20's more flexible here (despite having &quot;stronger&quot; factions) because there's more structure and framework to hang lots of options on. The big difference is V20 takes place in a world that's on the edge of major upheaval, where V5 takes place after the upheaval has happened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-10T08:29:53-07:00","id":1443366,"title":"","content":"FYI - Some people strongly prefer V20 because it's closer to the previous versions of the game.<br /> <br /> Others, like me, prefer V5.<br /> <br /> In the end, there's no objective answer and everyone here is a vampire fan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-10T08:43:22-07:00","id":1443367,"title":"","content":"I would say in V20 has better Blood Mechanics where you have a tank instead of an endless thirst and everyone can feed from everything.<br /> Thaumathurgy and other blood magic is better.<br /> No stupid Touchpointsystem for humanity.<br /> Dice checks are more calculatable because it is mostly against fix threshold instead of another dice.<br /> Thinbloods are not overpowered anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-10T13:16:46-07:00","id":1443392,"title":"","content":"For myself I would say the primary (perhaps only) advantage of 5th edition is that as of right now it's much better at avoiding coming off as reactionary and racist in it's lore. Though from what I can tell that trend seems to have started with some of obsidian path's entries to the v20 product line","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26738,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26738-queerpinko","user":"QueerPinko","date":". 04-10-2021, 04:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26738-queerpinko","name":"QueerPinko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-10T13:45:27-07:00","id":1443393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>QueerPinko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443318-how-would-you-get-a-v5-player-into-v20?p=1443392#post1443392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For myself I would say the primary (perhaps only) advantage of 5th edition is that as of right now it's much better at avoiding coming off as reactionary and racist in it's lore. Though from what I can tell that trend seems to have started with some of obsidian path's entries to the v20 product line</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, if we're talking about what advantages V5 have:<br /> <br /> * Update of the Banu Haqim<br /> * Update of the Ravnos<br /> * Update of the Ministry for more options<br /> * The removal of the Kuei-Jin (controversial but I think a good call)<br /> * Increased focus on humans<br /> * Increased focus on Hunters<br /> * A much better Humanity loss system so that vampires could theoretically kill hundreds of people over the years instead of dropping like a stone to wassail.<br /> * Loresheets are pretty cool.<br /> * The brokennss of Celerity has been resolved.<br /> * Blood Sorcery is not quite as One Discipline to Rule them All as Thaumaturgy<br /> * It's very good if you like the Anarchs.<br /> * The OPP art (not the main book, I'll be honest) is really-really good.<br /> * Better cross-media platforming<br /> * Much better reasoning on linking generation to the &quot;purity&quot; of the blood you feed.<br /> * Blood Potency related to age is a good idea, just like it wa sin Requiem.<br /> * The Malkavian Flaw is fixed.<br /> * The Gangrel Flaw is fixed<br /> * Ventrue Flaw is made less harsh but still effective<br /> <br /> There's a lot good here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-10T14:21:59-07:00","id":1443396,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s an odd turnaround to have people wanting people to sell them on an older edition, to be honest.<br /> <br /> V20 is definitely broader in focus, and bigger in page count, as it is really just a compilation edition rather than having any particular focus. I personally find a lot of the mechanics to be a bit clunky and don\u2019t function especially well at simulating the themes outlined in text, or even in creating dynamic play. Combat can include a whole cascade of dice-pool rolling for little consequential effect, for example, and the blood mechanics are basically just power points to spend. The art is also pretty mixed, with the questionable policy of using Leif Jones\u2019 more comic strip style for the Clan illustrations as an example. The game is set up to feel more like an urban fantasy than a horror game. While some fans will enthuse about the inclusion of all the thirteen Clans (rather than the seven in V5....and V1 and V2) and all the bloodlines, it means that Storyteller has less creative control over setting/story development if you have players who also read the book with a nerdish intensity for absorbing all the canon lore at once. There is less mystery to the setting. <br /> <br /> I think V20 was a product of it\u2019s time. It communicated to WW fans that the game line was still alive, even when WW seemed not to be and it set out the trend of Anniversary books to follow, although it was originally intended to be \u2018final word\u2019 on the line as a large one-off, all inclusive book. V5 is also a product of its time, where creators were looking to revitalize the game by capturing the spirit of the provocative original edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 04-10-2021, 05:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018