"user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-10T15:10:07-07:00","id":1443410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>archderd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443318-how-would-you-get-a-v5-player-into-v20?p=1443409#post1443409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">there are some pretty contestable advantages in there</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep and we could argue em.<br /> <br /> But Edition Warring is outlawed on the forums.<br /> <br /> Some people prefer some things, other people prefer others. I could list what I don't like about V5 too. Because no one likes everything of any edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-10T15:33:38-07:00","id":1443413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>QueerPinko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443318-how-would-you-get-a-v5-player-into-v20?p=1443392#post1443392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For myself I would say the primary (perhaps only) advantage of 5th edition is that as of right now it's much better at avoiding coming off as reactionary and racist in it's lore. Though from what I can tell that trend seems to have started with some of obsidian path's entries to the v20 product line</div> </div> </div> </div>Um, huh?<br /> <br /> V5 has done some work to reduce the racist in the lore, but not much. Just like V20 did, and Revised did, and late 2e did. VtM (like the WoD in general) is a long serious of updates trying to get away from how ill-informed 1e was and how many hurtful stereotypes were codified into the setting. V5 Banu Hakim are still blood-thristy killers dominated by Muslim leaders, the Ministry is still a cult of corruption for a different negative stereotype about brown people, and the Ravnos are still trouble making wanderers. If you've never read 1e, 2e, Rev. and V20 and all the lore therein, you might not see them as that bad, but to those of us that have been around for a while, it just comes off as yet another coat of paint trying to cover up mold that's never just been cleaned up properly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443318-how-would-you-get-a-v5-player-into-v20?p=1443410#post1443410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep and we could argue em.</div> </div> </div> </div>And we have!<br /> <br /> But more importantly, the point of this thread is effectively, &quot;what would be appealing about V20 to someone that started with V5&quot; so just listing the stuff you like about V5 seems like... edging towards another thing we're not supposed to do here. None of that list is actually an answer to the OP's question.<br /> <br /> I think that will we want to avoid an edition war, acknowledging how contentious some of that list is, is also important to why a lot of people prefer V20 to V5. The Humanity mechanics, for example, are quite different. V20 offer's a much more consistent experience, and if your players don't like the Humanity Path there's other codified options. V5's approach is much more variable to the table because there are far more risks to Humanity outside a vampire's personal choices and regaining Humanity is much harder so one V5 game can make it easy to maintain Humanity 8 or 9 if you want to, while another could drop everyone to 1-2 within a few sessions regardless of what the characters were trying to do. As you say, different people have different preferences for which is more appealing. But why would someone go to V20 from V5? Because the older Humanity/Path mechanics don't have massive risks to your Humanity from external sources and focus more on the specific choices your character makes; which might be more preferable to V5's approach without getting into one being better than the other.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-10T15:36:29-07:00","id":1443414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443318-how-would-you-get-a-v5-player-into-v20?p=1443413#post1443413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that will we want to avoid an edition war, acknowledging how contentious some of that list is, is also important to why a lot of people prefer V20 to V5. The Humanity mechanics, for example, are quite different. V20 offer's a much more consistent experience, and if your players don't like the Humanity Path there's other codified options. V5's approach is much more variable to the table because there are far more risks to Humanity outside a vampire's personal choices and regaining Humanity is much harder so one V5 game can make it easy to maintain Humanity 8 or 9 if you want to, while another could drop everyone to 1-2 within a few sessions regardless of what the characters were trying to do. As you say, different people have different preferences for which is more appealing. But why would someone go to V20 from V5? Because the older Humanity/Path mechanics don't have massive risks to your Humanity from external sources and focus more on the specific choices your character makes; which might be more preferable to V5's approach without getting into one being better than the other.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oddly, I do think Humanity loss is much-much harder in V5 because the stains system give you a lot more leeway versus a dropping ten point system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-10T15:39:19-07:00","id":1443416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443318-how-would-you-get-a-v5-player-into-v20?p=1443410#post1443410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yep and we could argue em.<br /> <br /> But Edition Warring is outlawed on the forums.<br /> <br /> Some people prefer some things, other people prefer others. I could list what I don't like about V5 too. Because no one likes everything of any edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>then i think you're heavily misusing advantage.<br /> advantages are things it does better, you listed things it did different<br /> <br /> the things you listed have their advantages but aren't advantages in themselves.<br /> an increased focus on humans and hunters is not an advantage it's a preference.<br /> <br /> i know it's arguing semantics but i think it matters in this case","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-10T16:09:40-07:00","id":1443417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443318-how-would-you-get-a-v5-player-into-v20?p=1443414#post1443414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oddly, I do think Humanity loss is much-much harder in V5 because the stains system give you a lot more leeway versus a dropping ten point system.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're both dropping 10 point systems with a set of &quot;bad stuff&quot; that prompts drops, and then dice rolls to see what happens.<br /> <br /> V5 is &quot;nicer&quot; on Humanity loss when it comes to the &quot;mundane&quot; evils of violating Chronicle tenets, where 1 Stain is significant (and can be offset with a Conviction completely) while 2 Stains is supposed to be particularly nasty violation, and earning 3+ just from violating tenets gets hard to imagine what you'd even do. It's much harsher on vampire specific stuff; esp. Touchstones. If your vampire is caught in a bad situation (and V5 actively encourages STs to set these up) you character can get slammed with 3-6 Stains from a single scene thanks to vampire specific Stains, possibly putting you in impairment, Aggravated Willpower Damage, and increased Frenzy risk for the whole session unless you willingly drop Humanity to end the effect early (and of course, risk having it happen again).<br /> <br /> So, I go back to what I said. It's not about one being &quot;objectively&quot; better than the other. They do things differently. V20's rules are more codified and less subjective, which may be frustrating or fun depending on your group. But there's also pretty much no reason a V20 vampire is going to drop below Humanity 4 unless they're actively trying to be an evil scumbag. In V5, there's no safety net where small things stop being a risk to your Humanity. A V5 vampire that has 1 Stain at the end of every session because of some seemingly small violation of tenets will, eventually, fall to the Beast. At Humaniy 6 or 7 it's a very unlucky roll, and it might be infrequent enough that you could save up the XP to recover if you don't spend it on other stuff. But once the drop starts (or more likely after a bad session where they picked up more than 1 Stain) each drop gets more and more likely for the same thing.<br /> <br /> Again, not saying one does things in a specifically better way, but they're very different ways. Claiming that V5 makes Humanity loss harder to happen is basically leaving out a massive caveat of, &quot;if your ST doesn't want it to happen, because if they want it to happen, they can make it happen very easily.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-10T16:12:24-07:00","id":1443418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443318-how-would-you-get-a-v5-player-into-v20?p=1443344#post1443344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">V20 has simpler disciplines, simpler factions, simpler character creation, simpler humanity, simpler backgrounds, a more honest assessment of easier-to-use skills, but more complicated combat (House rules: Ignore initiative phase, and take half for damage/soak do a lot to cut down on combat, which is largely intuitive but very slow) I'd argue that the disciplines and factions are better written too, and though I acknowledge that's a subjective thing, it'd be a hill I'd die on.<br /> <br /> The only problem I'd say is that V20 presents all all the major clans and their disciplines as equal, when they're not. Without looking bloodline section of the book, you're shown 13 clans and all their disciplines, A new Camarilla player should only really look at 7 clans and the common disciplines (That they use if you want to be cut things down further) Protean and perhaps thaumaturgy. Looking at the Tzmisce is no good if you're wanting to play a cam game for the first time. Don't be fooled; the game might have a lot more disciplines than v5, but they're streamlined and so much easier to work with than the convoluted discipline system V5 has.<br /> <br /> The only thing V5 improves on is... uh... Disciplines are more balanced in comparison to eachother. One thing to consider is that V5 is very much a game that tries to liberate you; big overpowering organizations are weakened, there's lots of room to advance; anarchs are just as good, if not better than the cam; you can play a Tremere without having a giant fucking pyramid behind you. It certainly doesn't always work, since you had much more freedom with morality in prior editions, you weren't bound by touchstones, and you didn't have to worry nearly as much about discipline builds in prior editions, but the general gist is to make V5 politically 'Easy'. V1,2,3 and 20, however, give you the Jyhad; Push, push, struggle: You will always have elders trying to keep you down and when you're older you'll have plucky neonates trying to eat you to get up. The Camarilla is a hegemony and you'll only join the anarchs if you can't cut it. You're under pressure, and it's good.<br /> Also there's the Sabbat who're just super interesting.<br /> <br /> You might actually want to have a look at the first edition of vampire. It's not so big and intimidating as V20, but is fully compatible.</div> </div> </div> </div>How are the Disciplines and Humanity simpler in v20 may I ask? That seems to be the opposite from my perception.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-10T16:55:06-07:00","id":1443423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443318-how-would-you-get-a-v5-player-into-v20?p=1443418#post1443418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How are the Disciplines and Humanity simpler in v20 may I ask? That seems to be the opposite from my perception.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, and why do people think V5 doesn\u2019t have Jyhad? That is a constant through all editions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-10T17:22:02-07:00","id":1443426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443318-how-would-you-get-a-v5-player-into-v20?p=1443418#post1443418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How are the Disciplines and Humanity simpler in v20 may I ask? That seems to be the opposite from my perception.</div> </div> </div> </div>To try to answer, obviously not MWiS:<br /> <br /> V20 Disciplines are not really mechanically simpler on an individual power level. They're simpler because there's only one power per dot by default. You don't have to pick between options, and plan your picks to make sure you don't lock yourself out of powers you might want,<br /> <br /> Humanity is more of a shift in what's simple. V20's Humanity mechanics are very straightforward: &quot;if you commit a violation, roll your dice, then apply results.&quot; You don't have to pick Tenets, Convictions, Touchstones, and so on. You don't amass points that can result in penalties that you need to keep track of. What counts as a violation is more complicated because there's a large chart with a lot of room for interpretation (esp. for anything that's not on it). There's also a lot of fiddly bits that are adjacent to Humanity in how the Virtues work.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-10T17:34:26-07:00","id":1443427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443318-how-would-you-get-a-v5-player-into-v20?p=1443426#post1443426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To try to answer, obviously not MWiS:<br /> <br /> V20 Disciplines are not really mechanically simpler on an individual power level. They're simpler because there's only one power per dot by default. You don't have to pick between options, and plan your picks to make sure you don't lock yourself out of powers you might want,<br /> <br /> Humanity is more of a shift in what's simple. V20's Humanity mechanics are very straightforward: &quot;if you commit a violation, roll your dice, then apply results.&quot; You don't have to pick Tenets, Convictions, Touchstones, and so on. You don't amass points that can result in penalties that you need to keep track of. What counts as a violation is more complicated because there's a large chart with a lot of room for interpretation (esp. for anything that's not on it). There's also a lot of fiddly bits that are adjacent to Humanity in how the Virtues work.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is more of a question of organization really.<br /> <br /> In V5, there are less Disciplines, with some of the effects being integrated into a smaller set of Disciplines accordingly. This means that more than one effect is given as an option to PCs for each respective level - it covers more ground. In V20, there is more effects overall largely because they list more Disciplines to cover all Clans.<br /> <br /> Similarly, Humanity as a ranking in V5 is meant as a more inclusively open measure of what Humanity means - which is why different vampires have different Tenets, Convictions and Touchstones - it reflects their own individual take as to what Humanity means. In V20, you had a more fixed meaning of Humanity (and fixed tenets), but then had lots of other alternative Paths to Humanity to choose. We have yet to see what happens in the upcoming Sabbat book, which is where alternative Paths to Humanity came from originally. However, current examples of previous Sabbat figures (mainly the Lasombra at this point) have Humanity scores, as defined by their own tenets. Because \u2018Humanity' can be built and used in a more bespoke way, the need for lots of alternative Paths becomes slightly redundant - although maybe you could have individuals rename \u2018Humanity\u2019 to something else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 04-10-2021, 08:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-11T02:38:21-07:00","id":1443453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443318-how-would-you-get-a-v5-player-into-v20?p=1443393#post1443393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, if we're talking about what advantages V5 have:<br /> <br /> * Update of the Banu Haqim<br /> * Update of the Ravnos<br /> * Update of the Ministry for more options<br /> * The removal of the Kuei-Jin (controversial but I think a good call)<br /> * Increased focus on humans<br /> * Increased focus on Hunters<br /> * A much better Humanity loss system so that vampires could theoretically kill hundreds of people over the years instead of dropping like a stone to wassail.<br /> * Loresheets are pretty cool.<br /> * The brokennss of Celerity has been resolved.<br /> * Blood Sorcery is not quite as One Discipline to Rule them All as Thaumaturgy<br /> * It's very good if you like the Anarchs.<br /> * The OPP art (not the main book, I'll be honest) is really-really good.<br /> * Better cross-media platforming<br /> * Much better reasoning on linking generation to the &quot;purity&quot; of the blood you feed.<br /> * Blood Potency related to age is a good idea, just like it wa sin Requiem.<br /> * The Malkavian Flaw is fixed.<br /> * The Gangrel Flaw is fixed<br /> * Ventrue Flaw is made less harsh but still effective<br /> <br /> There's a lot good here.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, no, no. You should write for the perspective of the OP, who has played V5 and that is his reference point to look at V20, don't do it the other way round<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">* Banu Haquim: The Assamites (who aren't called the Banu Haquim, which is a very strange name for them given half of them hate Haquim and the other half reject the influence of Islam) were a clan with three bloodlines and a rich history; with some converts, they formed a sect. This sect recently had a schism when a Methuselah woke up and told them to purge foreign religions and worship haquim and diablerie or die. The Sorcerer caste excluded the other castes from practicing magic; Quietus was a discipline for all Assamites, concerning poisons, and was most-certainly not just a form of sorcery. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">* Ravnos are just a different clan, one with an absolutely intriguing philosophy and sociological/pshychological stance </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">* Ministry: The Followers of set are a far more realized and grounded cult than the two farcical extremes we have of them in V5. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">* Asian vampires: A different species of vampires exists in Asia, who are more -angry spirit brings possesses corpse- than the blood lineages of western vampires. There's a lot of really interesting mechanics and philosophies behind them, but also some... eh... 90's isms. V20 isn't racist, though some of the first inclusions of these guys are questionable at best. V20 honestly doesn't touch these guys much. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">* Decreased focus on humans; some vampires are going to be very close to humans, whilst others view them as food. Unlike in V5, You have a choice. (which makes sense to me, because part of the vampire experience is the dehumanization of humans and the view that they're all cattle) </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">* Far more realistic attitude towards Hunters, who are fringe extremists for the most part and thus much smaller in scale. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">* Morality: Far more intuitive and far more personal. There are extreme philosophies to replace humanity for some vampires. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">* No lore sheets, however, there's a lot more freedom in choosing backgrounds and advantages and disadvantages</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">* Celerity is pretty broke, though it must be said the physical disciplines are more 'natural' and less a weird collection of very specific powers, also it's pretty easy to houserule this one very basic discipline. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">* Sorcery is treated like magic, with multiple paths and rituals, with vastly expanded capabilities; balanced by time, the need for a tutor, and XP investment. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">* Anarchs are, for the most part, dissident camarilla, except for a few places where they're actively rebeling. The Camarilla is a competent global organization. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">* Better art. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">* Have you heard of VTM:Bloodlines? Great game. Go play that. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">* Generation is much more consistent, both mechanically and from the point of view of some esoteric philosophies. <br /> * Diablerie is something you do to to raise your limits, it's not a quick and dirty path to a bunch of XP, and is far more balanced as a result. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">* The Malkavian Flaw is... worse. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">* The Gangrel Flaw is different. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">* Ventrue Flaw is harsher. <br /> * The Tzmisce are much, much, much better. Their unique discipline certainly makes them stand out, and their discipline spread matches the culture of the clan much better than V5. <br /> * The Lasombra are Much, much, much better; Obtenebration is stronger than oblivion (arguably too strong), and they aren't prostrating themselves to join an imploding Camarilla like in V5; they're the kings of the Sabbat, with a few elites secretly in the Camarilla. <br /> -The Clan of death is the Giovanni, a collection of incestuous families with Potence, Dominate and Necromancy. Necromancy, like thaumaturgy, is actually-like-magic pre-v5. There are several other necromancy Bloodlines with very different spreads and very different playstyles and politics. While it's implied that these families will eventually rebel against the main family, which is done in V5, there's no way all these bloodlines will come together to form one clan, specially because one of them is a Followers of Set Bloodline.<br /> * The Brujah are in the Cam, because they'd never leave the cam. </span></span></span><br /> * The Beast is something you can control if you're smart about it; Placate the beast, keep it well fed, keep yourself out of danger and it won't trouble you &quot;The Beast I am Lest a Beast I Become&quot;. There are no hunger complications or messy criticals, either you're in control or the Beast is, there's no gray area or 'The Beast made me do it&quot;. You are responsible for keeping your beast in check. If you frenzy, it was because you were dumb enough to put yourself in the wrong situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-11T03:40:58-07:00","id":1443459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443318-how-would-you-get-a-v5-player-into-v20?p=1443427#post1443427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this is more of a question of organization really.<br /> <br /> In V5, there are less Disciplines, with some of the effects being integrated into a smaller set of Disciplines accordingly. This means that more than one effect is given as an option to PCs for each respective level - it covers more ground. In V20, there is more effects overall largely because they list more Disciplines to cover all Clans.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it isn't just organization.<br /> <br /> If I want to play a Lasombra that wishes to master the manipulation of shadows and summoning ghosts? In V20 I buy Obtenebration and Necromancy. In V5 I find a different concept because that is mechanically impossible thanks to Obtenebration and Necromancy being folded into one Discipline of which I only get 5 total powers (plus in this specific example a few rituals, but those all have specific powers as prerequisites, unlike Blood Sorcery that at least lets you buy as many rituals as you want to make up for the more limited options of what five powers you take).<br /> <br /> If V5 worked like pre-V5's Combo Disciplines or Elder (6+) Disciplines where you can buy the extra powers you don't pick up by increasing your rating in the Discipline with more XP? Then it would more be a matter of organization with a slight bit of preference on a few small factors.<br /> <br /> As it stands, this goes back to my first post. V20 is more flexible. It lets me build the vampire I want to build. Nothing is mechanically walled off from my character, but rather some things will take considerable in-play actions to get. V5 is more restrictive because it wants a specific feel. In this case it wants vampires to feel more diverse in how the blood expresses itself so not every character that learns a given Discipline will manifest it the same way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-11T04:05:49-07:00","id":1443460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443318-how-would-you-get-a-v5-player-into-v20?p=1443459#post1443459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, it isn't just organization.<br /> <br /> If I want to play a Lasombra that wishes to master the manipulation of shadows and summoning ghosts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't you just mix your powers up?<br /> <br /> But yes, I feel like you should be able to buy multiple levels of every Discipline.<br /> <br /> It and the lack of Elder Disciplines are my biggest issues with V5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-11T04:38:23-07:00","id":1443462,"title":"","content":"Lore-wise I play in the revised era (most of my games are around the early 2000s), rules-wise I play V5. After playing this game for over 20 years, V5 is much easier on my players, especially new ones. Many aspects of the vampire are now part of the system and it's cool, and horrifying which is what I am looking for in this game. <br /> <br /> Would I play 20th? of course. It's amazing. I love it to death. I am using this book and the old clan books more than I am using the V5 book. I just prefer the rules, and character creation, and powers, and humanity, and blood system of V5 better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24461-godforsaken","name":"Godforsaken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24461_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-11T04:52:48-07:00","id":1443463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443318-how-would-you-get-a-v5-player-into-v20?p=1443459#post1443459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If V5 worked like pre-V5's Combo Disciplines or Elder (6+) Disciplines where you can buy the extra powers you don't pick up by increasing your rating in the Discipline with more XP? Then it would more be a matter of organization with a slight bit of preference on a few small factors.</div> </div> </div> </div>You gain a new power for every dot - from anything with a level equal or below the Discipline rating. So you could have both the 1st level powers instead of an extra 2nd level power when you get an additional dot. It\u2019s not directly for an XP cost although a ST could tweak a house rule it that you simply pay the XP cost of a new Discipline level to buy extra powers - and provide some more Amalgam powers if you wanted to expand out that idea further too. For me, it is still about an organizational shift more than anything else - because the system as it is can still be customized and built up, with lots of options already as it stands.<br /> <br /> However, I also felt that V20 had too many traits like Disciplines and the whole 'building a vampire power-set exactly how you want\u2019 aspect is a bit like 'building any superhero you want\u2019 in Champions to me. I can see the appeal, but for me personally, it detracts from actually wanting to play a vampire, in terms of the personal condition and tragedy-story elements, towards the drive for playing a superpowered being with a vampire meta-overlay. The issue does go to the core of the debate between V5 and V20 though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-11T05:35:05-07:00","id":1443466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443318-how-would-you-get-a-v5-player-into-v20?p=1443460#post1443460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't you just mix your powers up?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mixing them up just results in a master of none situation. If you want to summon and bind ghosts, you need The Binding Fetter (also Auspex 1), Where the Shroud Thins, and Necrotic Plague (because most of this is actually in the rituals, not the powers you're picking). You probably want Oblivion's Sight even though it's not strictly necessary because you might want to be able to see ghosts if you're going to be dealing with them as a major thing you do. There's no pick of two shadow manipulation powers that's going to make you feel like a &quot;master&quot; of doing that after you have your ghost summoning and binding dealt with, and you're really only getting one if you want to feel like a master of ghosts and thus take the fourth power to see them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443318-how-would-you-get-a-v5-player-into-v20?p=1443463#post1443463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You gain a new power for every dot - from anything with a level equal or below the Discipline rating.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, which inherently locks you out of other powers in that Discipline permanently, because you only get five even if you can spend them in multiple ways.<br /> <br /> Calling this an &quot;organizational&quot; issue just doesn't hold water. It's not how the powers are organized, it's that you only get five of them, ever, and there's always more than five options, so you're always going to end up denying yourself access to some of the powers in a Discipline.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I can see the appeal, but for me personally, it detracts from actually wanting to play a vampire, in terms of the personal condition and tragedy-story elements, towards the drive for playing a superpowered being with a vampire meta-overlay. The issue does go to the core of the debate between V5 and V20 though. </div> </div> </div>This of course, as usual, skips the idea of play focused on the temptations of power. <br /> <br /> The line between &quot;superheroes with fangs&quot; and &quot;the power of vamprism is an insidious trap,&quot; is mostly in the the enforcement and execution of the downsides of being a vampire. But you can't make the temptations of being a vampire be a trap if the power fantasy aspect isn't there. It's very hard to do the whole, &quot;young vampires think they're masters of the kine, and lords of the night, but those that survive quickly learn that the Curse of Caine takes far more than it gives,&quot; if you can't make characters that you can see feeling drunk on the power of being a vampire for a while, so when the flaws in the deal start to kick them in the teeth, it hits harder than vampires feeling completely cursed from night one, and their few powers never feeling like it was worth it.<br /> <br /> So, again, as I said in my opening, a reason to go V20 is better support for multiple playstyles and approaches to the game. Because again, we're not here to argue why V5 is good, we're here to answer what about V20 would make someone consider trying it or adopting it after starting with V5.<br /> <br /> --------------<br /> <br /> Also, for the sake of the thread, can we please not do the &quot;but house rules!&quot; thing?<br /> <br /> House rules are a wash. House rules don't change that V20 has overwrought combat mechanics. House rules don't change that Convictions have to be linked to a specific Touchstone that represents that Conviction in the eyes of the vampire instead of allowing them to more broadly support a vampire's human side. Or any of the other things people on both sides of V20 vs V5 tend to agree are flaws in either game.<br /> <br /> Neither game is more or less capable of being fixed with house rules; it's just how much energy you're willing to put into the game you're playing to address any issues you come across.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-11T10:02:41-07:00","id":1443477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443318-how-would-you-get-a-v5-player-into-v20?p=1443344#post1443344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but more complicated combat (House rules: Ignore initiative phase, and take half for damage/soak do a lot to cut down on combat, which is largely intuitive but very slow)<br /> <br /> You might actually want to have a look at the first edition of vampire. It's not so big and intimidating as V20, but is fully compatible.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I agree with most of what you wrote you lost me with the above, I wouldn't use that house rule and isn't first edition the worst version of balance/rules/combat? If I am remembering right the target number for damaging your opponent is their Stamina + 3? pretty easy to make them botch the damage roll as often as they do damage to be soaked, talk about long fights. I love the feel of first edition, the adventure in the back with Gary, the cartoon, Etc... but we went right to second edition to clean things up (and because first edition fell apart if you breathed at it too hard while turning the page).<br /> <br /> I think second edition even had the same adventure and comic strip in it though it's been too long to remember for sure. I remember it being basically the same stuff cleaned up a bit. Overall I would recommend V20 myself but Second edition over the first for rules sake if you want to go back. I remember Flesh of Marble making you unstakeable requiring 10 successes after the half and it being always active in first edition. Some of those level 6 Auspex powers were truly useless compared to others. First is really just a beta test.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-11T12:55:14-07:00","id":1443496,"title":"","content":"One thing I do like about V20 and prior is difficulties. In V20, 4 dice means you're competent, in v5, without house rules, 6 dice means you're competent, 4 dice will fail you most normal tasks without willpower expenditure. The classic vampire really enables diverse skills while the V5 method really pigeonholes you. <br /> <br /> It's been said above, but V20's disciplines are better for a number of reasons. <br /> First, simplicity. V5 presents us with too much choice; not only do you need to pick your Discipline but you've got to pick your powers within that power, and you have to pick carefuly because you can't have everything and you have to actively plan out a career path and choose which powers you will never have. Also you need some other disciplines for combinations so you can't get X3 without first getting Y2. That's a headache. V20 might give us 20 disciplines instead of 7, but you can compartmentalize easier; you know you'll never get obtenebration so you can comfortably shut it out of your mind, nor will you get Chimestry anytime soon. When you get Auspex 1, you're not excluding yourself from any auspex power, you can get every 1-5 auspex power simply by going from level 1-5. <br /> Second, most common disiplines are in a very logical order. The extreme may be the physical disciplines like Potence, where level 1 gives you +1 strength and level 2 gives you +2 strength, but there's also a good deal of logic in the advancement of, say, Dominate, where you have a word they must obey, a sentence they must obey, memory alteration, complete brainwashing, and finaly you deprive them of control over their own bodies and take their action for them through possession. This makes Disciplines much easier to remember and makes them more like a vampiric extention of power rather than just a bunch of powers put together for a game. <br /> Third; If you want a simple fun vampire and don't want to think too much, a Brujah gives you very simple mechanics; Potence and Celerity are very very simple, meaning you only need to remember what things do for Presence, but If you want to go nerd hard into some complexity, you can pick up a Tremere and have lots of different paths and rituals. V5... well, A Brujah is only slightly less complicated than a Tremere, because Potence and Celerity are now as complicated as any other discipline and Sorcery is as complicated as any other discipline but also has the benefit of rituals. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vamps Like Us</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443318-how-would-you-get-a-v5-player-into-v20?p=1443477#post1443477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While I agree with most of what you wrote you lost me with the above,.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, say I'm using a pistol (4 base damage) and I roll Dex+Firearms and hit a vampire with 3 successes, ordinarily I'd have 6 dice to roll damage, and the let's say the vampire had 4 dice to soak. Rather than have myself roll 6 dice and the vampire roll 4, which could be absurdly lethal or possitively harmless, the six dice becomes 3 damage and the 4 dice of soak becomes two levels of soak, and the character takes 1 level of damage. Three rolls (four, if the vampire bothered to dodge) becomes 1 (or 2 if bothering to dodge). Combat is nearly twice as fast, and also we're reducing the absurd luck that sometimes occurs when rolling damage (I've seen 14 dice do nothing) <br /> Round up. <br /> If I do have to roll damage/soak (say, someone has a power that effects how hard it is to soak, such as the werewolf gift acid talons, or we're simply dealing with something like fire or electricity) I don't count 1's or 0's. That also reduces the amount of BS.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-11T13:39:10-07:00","id":1443503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443318-how-would-you-get-a-v5-player-into-v20?p=1443460#post1443460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But yes, I feel like you should be able to buy multiple levels of every Discipline.<br /> <br /> It and the lack of Elder Disciplines are my biggest issues with V5.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree and disagree. I don't really miss the &quot;only Kryptonite can save you now&quot; elder Disciplines. Vampire demigods never &quot;clicked&quot; with me. But allowing elders to trade ridiculous levels of power for great versatility seems like a sensible approach to creating formidable yet not invincible elder characters to me.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/100-jezmiller","name":"JezMiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-11T14:10:40-07:00","id":1443506,"title":"","content":"Elders being terrifying is great. Paranoia and uphill battles, constantly struggling for your existence; That's what makes a great vampire game. I don't think Vampire did a particularly great job at writing powers at levels 7 though to 9, but it was great that powers 7 through to 9 existed, and the same goes for raising your attributes and skills beyond 5; it was a great motivator for trying to work up.<br /> <br /> Elders in V5... I'm not sure if they didn't think it through or knew what they were doing and decided to do it anyway. Blood Potency above 5* is a lot of trouble, to the point where you should absolutely not allow yourself to have that much potency. There are benefits, sure, but the drawbacks are suicidal. Diablerie in V5 is a quick and dirty route for XP, not a path to transcending your limitations and becoming less mundane and more divine, not a curse to keep the Cainite race at eachother's throats; it's literally just a method for which you trade humanity dots for discipline dots, discipline dots your character would get anyway if they'd just farmed resonances like you might be supposed to.<br /> <br /> Elders in V5 just aren't a force to be reckened with; half of them have been beckoned, the remainder are stronger than individual players but far weaker than a coterie or a coterie-sized bunch of hunters. They don't pressure PCs like they used to. Just shifting powers around doesn't really help them much. 'versatility' itself is not strength. Strength is strength. Elders in V5 become Jacks of all trades and they heal frighteningly fast but they don't become the dragons they were and you don't really have much incentive to conflict with them nor do they have much incentive to cause trouble with you, since you'd only try to eat your way towards caine in v5 if you were mentally deficient enough to not-be-embraced. Strong blood potency just lowers your quality of life as it puts you too much at the mercy of your beast and reduces the value of your favourite food sources. In V20 taking a particular elder down and getting away with it can be a chronicle, in V5 it's an episode. This in turn calls into question the motivations of the Sabbat, the Assamite loyalists, and any other group with an eye for generation.<br /> <br /> V20: Push, Push, Struggle. (80's!!)<br /> V5: Be happy with just the way you are, because trying to have more will just hurt you. Maybe fight some inept fascists (Camarilla, Church of Set, Assamite Loyalists..) for a power fantasy or fight hunters for a persecution fantasy.<br /> In V20 you're fighting up or down, in V5 you're fighting across the isle. I don't think what V5 is doing here is bad in a vacuum it's just not as good as what V20 is doing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-11T15:18:13-07:00","id":1443518,"title":"","content":"I think there are ways to do Elder Disciplines without getting into the 6+ powers area, though it would still require changing V5's rules to accomplish.<br /> <br /> Something Vampire the Requiem does (though a bit of an edge case over there) to accomplish this are basically just having custom powers that follow the same basic formula as normal Devotions (aka Combo Disciplines aka Amalgams) but have Blood Potency requirements to create/learn. The end result isn't inherently all that different from Elder Disciplines (high BP characters have access to powers lesser vampires can't unless they fight their way up the ladder first, and they're more individual and variable than the normal Discipline progression), but the logic of designing and rating them is easier; resulting in a more consistent power level to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-11T17:50:37-07:00","id":1443542,"title":"","content":"For the specific example of the shadow-manipulating necromancer above, you could always take the Abyssal Apprentice Merit from the Descendant of Montano Loresheet and select your reliably available Oblivion powers based on which Ceremonies you want constant access to. There's not an equivalent published loresheet I'm aware of that does the same for Hecata characters, but I'd think such would be less interested in traditional Lasombra areas of expertise anyway. And the precedent is set, both for similar custom loresheet Merits available to other clans and the implication that elders are able to master powers beyond the initial 5 in a given discipline. (With the most logical gateway to such being high dots of Blood Potency.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-11T20:00:15-07:00","id":1443554,"title":"","content":"I think that's a bit of a stretch.<br /> <br /> Abyssal Apprentice isn't written in a fashion that grants you Ceremonies since you haven't actually learned the power. You also only get to use the power once per story, which is hardly reliable or constant access. Occasionally having access to a single Oblivion power you don't possess isn't going to make a character feel like a master of ghosts and shadows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-11T23:05:49-07:00","id":1443566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443318-how-would-you-get-a-v5-player-into-v20?p=1443466#post1443466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Calling this an &quot;organizational&quot; issue just doesn't hold water. It's not how the powers are organized, it's that you only get five of them, ever, and there's always more than five options, so you're always going to end up denying yourself access to some of the powers in a Discipline.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is literally an issue of how each edition organizes its Disciplines, so whether you like it or not, it is an organizational issue. Like I say, if you rule it that you can buy powers at the cost of a Discipline dot, then there is no reason why you can\u2019t have more than five powers. I guess that this is just a house rule but the spirit of V5 is that the game <i>isn\u2019t</i> designed to be driven by a catalogue of powers - and it isn\u2019t a problem for me personally - so it is just a solution to the issue outlined here and, as such it would need to be a house rule as it stands. Who knows, though, whenever V5 gets around to having an Elders sourcebook, they may end up ruling it themselves as it is seamless enough to implement.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This of course, as usual, skips the idea of play focused on the temptations of power.<br /> <br /> The line between &quot;superheroes with fangs&quot; and &quot;the power of vamprism is an insidious trap,&quot; is mostly in the the enforcement and execution of the downsides of being a vampire. But you can't make the temptations of being a vampire be a trap if the power fantasy aspect isn't there. It's very hard to do the whole, &quot;young vampires think they're masters of the kine, and lords of the night, but those that survive quickly learn that the Curse of Caine takes far more than it gives,&quot; if you can't make characters that you can see feeling drunk on the power of being a vampire for a while, so when the flaws in the deal start to kick them in the teeth, it hits harder than vampires feeling completely cursed from night one, and their few powers never feeling like it was worth it.<br /> <br /> So, again, as I said in my opening, a reason to go V20 is better support for multiple playstyles and approaches to the game. Because again, we're not here to argue why V5 is good, we're here to answer what about V20 would make someone consider trying it or adopting it after starting with V5. </div> </div> </div>Well 'temptations of power\u2019 isn\u2019t much of a theme if there are no downsides to it - it is just an excuse to play out a power fantasy. All fine in a game like D&amp;D or Champions, or whathaveyou, but the Vampire game is billed as being a game of personal horror. If the powers outweigh the downside of vampiric existence in the game, it ceases to be a horror game. And again, this is<i> just my view </i>- but I fundamentally believe that losing <i>any</i> notion of \u2019superheroes with fangs\u2019 in V:TM is <i>a good thing</i>. I flatly do not value it as a play style that Vampire needs to support - there are other games better adapted for that sort of thing.<br /> <br /> Moreover, the PCs still get powers, but the Disciples system is organized in a different way. If people want to play that out as a theme - \u2019temptations of power\u2019 - it is still a possibility. It just doesn\u2019t work the way it used to. I know the players in my group are enthused by the powers their characters have at their disposal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 04-12-2021, 06:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-12T03:58:58-07:00","id":1443576,"title":"","content":"The thing with disciplines in V5 is that every dot, even if you took a level 1 power, increases the dice pool of the entire discipline and makes the whole package more powerful. A level 1 fortitude power taken as the 5th dot will increase your fortitude dice pool from 4 to 5 and will give you 5 boxes of health. This is quite amazing. So I don't think players should pay less if they take &quot;lower&quot; powers. Because those powers are quite powerful the more dots you have in the discipline.<br /> <br /> All in all the updated disciplines did more good than bad, especially with fortitude, potence, and celerity, my players love the customization and options they have with each discipline, animalism comes to mind, and presence, I love it in V5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24461-godforsaken","name":"Godforsaken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24461_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-12T06:20:02-07:00","id":1443587,"title":"","content":"Another thing that V20 and prior excelled at was that the factions pulled you towards diverse, interesting and challenging philosophies. V5 has stripped it down to a dichotomy of order and freedom, with some heavy overtones of mortal politics; The Anarchs are champions of liberty, The Camarilla champion conservatism; The Ministry of Set Champion Freedom, The Church of Set Champion control; House Tremere champions tradition, House Carna celebrates deviancy. Factions are all yings and yangs, sometimes to the point of caricature: both church and ministry would be considered heretical extemes by the original Followers of Set which they stem from, but there's no middle-ground orthadox possition in line with what 90% of the followers believed before the split. It's very partisan.<br /> <br /> V20 didn't do that; The Anarchs weren't the polar opposite of the Camarilla, and nor where the other major sect that went missing between editions, the Sabbat. Each side had their merits and flaws, they seemed natural, politically and sociologically viable*. They didn't feel tailor made to someone's viewpoint, and it was an interesting challenge to conform and wrap yourself around the ideals of your sect, where you are somewhat encouraged to play characters that don't have the same opinion as you rather than indulge in your comfort zone (playing a character with the same opinion as you is fine, but you gotta be smart about it, and that 'being smart about it' creates intriuge. Every major and minor sect has very interesting ideas that move beyond the scope of simply mortal politics run vicariously through vampires (Though I must admit V5's sections on feudal cities were pretty good)<br /> <br /> *The Sabbat seem dysfunctional at first glance, but are evidently viable the more you read/understand the context in which they commit most of their crimes)<br /> <br /> Speaking of philosophies, outside the camarilla (a few are inside) a vampire can choose to completely abandon the morality of Humanity and instead choose to follow a faith,creed or philosophy more amenable to their undead situation. Be it an outdated concept of chivalry, a dream of obtaining a state beyond vampirism, the idea that vampires are demons sent by god to test humanity and should act like it, an aim to become in tune with their beast, or dedicating their whole being to the god Set; Vampires can completely run up the wall with alien mindsets and strange ideas and can truly become monsters or at least interesting. This system of paths is also good in that they're set mechanically, so you're not doomed to haggling with your storyteller over convictions and chronicle tenets, though the concept is broad enough that you could adjust paths if you can agree to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 04-12-2021, 11:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-12T06:22:04-07:00","id":1443588,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">A reminder this is about how to get a 5th Edition player into V20 not to complain about V5 or talk about V20 or V5 is better. I was guilty of this myself.</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Edit:<br /> <br /> Because everyone has been good for the past year:</span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...-vs-v20-thread</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-12-2021, 10:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-12T22:07:35-07:00","id":1443702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443318-how-would-you-get-a-v5-player-into-v20?p=1443588#post1443588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">A reminder this is about how to get a 5th Edition player into V20 not to complain about V5 or talk about V20 or V5 is better. I was guilty of this myself.</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Edit:<br /> <br /> Because everyone has been good for the past year:</span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443592-the-official-v5-vs-v20-thread\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...-vs-v20-thread</a></div> </div> </div> </div>What this said. I just wanted to know what v20 had to offer since I started strongly with v5. I didn't want opinions on v5, because I already love it. I also didn't want to start arguments about which edition is better, just solid opinions. After all, these are games we play and enjoy as a community right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-13T05:23:04-07:00","id":1443727,"title":"","content":"I actually enjoy V20's character creation, whilst V5's character creation is... cumbersome. But credit where it's due, the V5 character creation system is more balanced. The primary issue is v20 letting you allocate dots relatively freely while also charging incrementally higher XP rates as you go up a level. So with Attributes costing 4x current level in v20, but the ability to allocate 7/5/3 dots as you please, it's much better to do something like 5/4/1 , 4/3/1, 4/1/1 rather than something more balanced like 4/3/3, 3/3/2, 2/2/2. Let's take the 4/1/1 VS 2/2/2. If you wanted 4/2/2, it'd take the optimiser 8xp, and the balanced character 20xp, and this adds up significantly when you do it to the entire character sheet. The way V5 does things prevents such abuse, but it is a bit too regimented and difficult and plainly doesn't grant the freedom of V20. A more elegant sollution would be to cancel the incrimentally higher XP rates for attributes and abilities, but I must say I like incrementals for disciplines, and V5's system of 2/1/0 for disciplines is a very good idea (Though it gets screwed up by predator types offering an additional discipline dot, because 3/1/0, 2/2/0 and 2/1/1 are not equal in XP) <br /> While V5 has an interesting system in advantages (IE it's restrictive but that cuts down on the bullshit players pull) I do like v20's system of 15 freebies and merits/flaws, even if that's not very balanced and encourages the players to spend far too long working out how to best optimise merits and flaws. Also, quite plainly, some of the merits and flaws are broke, and I've had players tell me they always pick X because it's free points and it's not like it'd effect them anyway (I don't allow a lot of them)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-13T05:45:35-07:00","id":1443731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443318-how-would-you-get-a-v5-player-into-v20?p=1443727#post1443727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While V5 has an interesting system in advantages (IE it's restrictive but that cuts down on the bullshit players pull) I do like v20's system of 15 freebies and merits/flaws, even if that's not very balanced and encourages the players to spend far too long working out how to best optimise merits and flaws. Also, quite plainly, some of the merits and flaws are broke, and I've had players tell me they always pick X because it's free points and it's not like it'd effect them anyway (I don't allow a lot of them)</div> </div> </div> </div>The merits and flaws system in V5 is bad, and mostly because of lack of options, the selection is tiny, and really not that interesting. I am missing the v20's selection of merits and flaws. It was amazing. I don't mind that backgrounds and merits are kinda the same, that's cool. Just give me more options! you had all those ideas in previous editions. Where are they?!?!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24461-godforsaken","name":"Godforsaken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24461_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-13T08:17:36-07:00","id":1443747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443318-how-would-you-get-a-v5-player-into-v20?p=1443566#post1443566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is literally an issue of how each edition organizes its Disciplines, so whether you like it or not, it is an organizational issue. Like I say, if you rule it that you can buy powers at the cost of a Discipline dot, then there is no reason why you can\u2019t have more than five powers. I guess that this is just a house rule but the spirit of V5 is that the game <i>isn\u2019t</i> designed to be driven by a catalogue of powers - and it isn\u2019t a problem for me personally - so it is just a solution to the issue outlined here and, as such it would need to be a house rule as it stands. Who knows, though, whenever V5 gets around to having an Elders sourcebook, they may end up ruling it themselves as it is seamless enough to implement.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is patently absurd in such a way I find hard to believe:<br /> <br /> If you need to (house)rule that you can have more than five powers, then you can't have more than five powers. RAW. Wheter you like it or not, V5 clearly states it's not an orgtanizational matter but a matter of how many powers you're allowed to play with<br /> <br /> That you - <i>assuming you're the ST</i> - as owner of the game and the table, can do whatever you want in spite of what V5 says, doen't make it a mere organizational matter. <i>If you're not the ST, and the ST likes the way V5 does stuff, <b>then you can't rule shit</b></i><br /> <br /> In forums where what RAW says actually matters, this would have gotten you banned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-13T11:39:30-07:00","id":1443766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443318-how-would-you-get-a-v5-player-into-v20?p=1443702#post1443702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What this said. I just wanted to know what v20 had to offer since I started strongly with v5. I didn't want opinions on v5, because I already love it. I also didn't want to start arguments about which edition is better, just solid opinions. After all, these are games we play and enjoy as a community right?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's well and good, but it's honestly a bit hard say '20th has this which V5 doesn't&quot; without, you know... making comparisons. <br /> <br /> My 'opinions' for a few things that make V20 worth picking up. <br /> -Vampires are more powerful in V20; Ancient vampires are much stronger than young vampires, who are much stronger than mortals. There's a lot more verticality and it's great for playing plucky underdogs or indulging in the occasional power fantasy. <br /> -Obfuscate and Dominate is really, really fun in V20. V5 clamped down on them in the name of balance, but here they're unhinged wonders ready to stomp all over your enemies. There's so much creativity you can pull off with these badboys in V20. <br /> -Combat in V20 is less abstract and more simulationist. I like that a lot. It's a lot more tactical and if you're big into fighting IRL you can choose to get nitty-gritty with grapples and such. It's quite intuitive so that's a big plus, but slow without houserules<br /> -A chill metaplot, crazy world shaking things aren't happening all the time, leaving you to focus on your local setting and whatever's cooked up inside it. V20 is pretty timeless and works great whether you want to play in 68, 1068, 1568, 1968, 2068 or 2168. <br /> -More inter-sect politicing; V5 heavily emphasizes Red VS Blue, and while V20 certainly has that, a good chunk of your plots are going to be Camarilla Young VS Camarilla old, perhaps you'll join in on a plot to make someone the new prince or you'll uncover a cult which becomes a powder-keg. If you're in another sect, there's lots and lots of subfactions available for intrigue or infighting.<br /> -The Sabbat is a cocaine blender for when you're bored of pretending to care about humanity, but also a deep and nuanced... they're interesting. Very interesting. You'll have people at your table arguing that they're the good guys, when they're clearly not; That kind of interesting<br /> -I just like the way V20 does the beast better. I like control, messy criticals are not for me, and I think they make the setting/masquerade a bit suspect. V20 makes me more responsible. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-13T11:50:43-07:00","id":1443772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443318-how-would-you-get-a-v5-player-into-v20?p=1443747#post1443747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is patently absurd in such a way I find hard to believe:<br /> <br /> If you need to (house)rule that you can have more than five powers, then you can't have more than five powers. RAW. Wheter you like it or not, V5 clearly states it's not an orgtanizational matter but a matter of how many powers you're allowed to play with<br /> <br /> That you - <i>assuming you're the ST</i> - as owner of the game and the table, can do whatever you want in spite of what V5 says, doen't make it a mere organizational matter. <i>If you're not the ST, and the ST likes the way V5 does stuff, <b>then you can't rule shit</b></i><br /> <br /> In forums where what RAW says actually matters, this would have gotten you banned.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it is a matter of how the game organizes the powers, then it is an organizational matter. And, as a point of fact, the ST can do whatever they want with the game, and that is a stated rule in the game too.<br /> <br /> The issue is one for people on this thread, rather than being inherently bad - it is no advantage to me how V20 organizes its powers, for example - so the issue is only ever going to be house ruled to taste. As such, it is still a simple thing to make a ruling that allows players to spend points on extra powers, based on the cost of a new Discipline level. It isn\u2019t required to do so for anybody who is happy with the V5 rules, which operates on the basis of each Discipline forking into different powers to provide meaningful choices.<br /> <br /> Thankfully, we don\u2019t post in forums where RAW is such a matter that it would get people banned - because that would be ridiculous - and I have given the context of this rule suggestion twice now. What will get people banned is surreptitious attempts at edition warring, that we have all been warned about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 04-13-2021, 03:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-13T12:51:01-07:00","id":1443787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godforsaken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443318-how-would-you-get-a-v5-player-into-v20?p=1443731#post1443731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The merits and flaws system in V5 is bad, and mostly because of lack of options, the selection is tiny, and really not that interesting. I am missing the v20's selection of merits and flaws</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the base method of V5's approach to Merits and Flaws is actually better, but I agree heavily that it's extremely lacking; esp. since the game already cut back on a lot of base-line customization. The most variety and &quot;cool&quot; factor is moved to Loresheets, but if you find the perfect Merit on a Loresheet, but no interest in that Loresheet's lore... you're now at the whim of the ST on how to deal with that. Loresheets are a good idea (though as usual, since they didn't even change the name, I'm going to insist on acknowledging Legends of Wulin/Weapons of the Gods for actually creating the concept and name for them), but if your group isn't comfortable making their own (and there's no guideline for doing so) it makes getting some of that classic Merit/Flaw &quot;cool&quot; factor hard.<br /> <br /> So, relating this back to why to try out V20? If you want neat quirks to your character, instead of having to tie them to the parts of the lore/setting the designers have decided to say they're attached to, you pick the flavor quirks you want, and then decide how they are worked into the setting with your ST.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-13T13:12:50-07:00","id":1443795,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>I think this got into Edition Warring. I contributed and am sorry. So, sadly, we must shut it down.</b></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}